---
import SubpageLayout from '../../layouts/SubpageLayout.astro';
---

<SubpageLayout title="Plan Your Visit" description="Everything you need to know about travelling to the Republic of Nauru — visas, money, transport, accommodation, climate and the practical realities on the ground." sectionEmoji="✈️" sectionLabel="Travel Guide" includeFooter={true}>
  <p>Nauru is tiny, remote and wonderfully unusual. That combination makes trip planning straightforward once the basics are clear — but the basics matter. This page brings together the essential travel decisions you need to make before you book.</p>
  <div class="callout-grid">
    <a href="/visit/visa/" class="callout"><h3>Visa first</h3><p>Start with entry requirements and timing.</p></a>
    <a href="/visit/accommodation/" class="callout"><h3>Book stay early</h3><p>Availability can be more important than price.</p></a>
    <a href="/visit/transport/" class="callout"><h3>Arrival flow</h3><p>Understand the airport, transfers, and island transport.</p></a>
    <a href="/visit/currency/" class="callout"><h3>Cash & payments</h3><p>Budgeting matters on a small remote island.</p></a>
  </div>

  <h2>Before you go</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Topic</th><th>What to decide</th><th>Why it matters</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Visa</td><td>Check entry rules and processing times</td><td>Applications can take weeks</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Accommodation</td><td>Reserve a room before booking flights</td><td>Choice is limited</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Money</td><td>Bring sufficient cash and backup payment options</td><td>ATMs/cards can be unreliable</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Packing</td><td>Light clothing, sun protection, rain cover</td><td>Tropical weather changes quickly</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Practical planning checklist</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Check passport validity and visa rules.</li>
    <li>Book accommodation before finalising flights.</li>
    <li>Plan a cash budget for food, transport and small extras.</li>
    <li>Prepare for limited connectivity with offline copies of key documents.</li>
    <li>Download maps, confirmations and essentials before arrival.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Explore the detailed guides</h2>
  <div class="link-grid">
    <a href="/visit/visa/">Visa requirements</a>
    <a href="/visit/weather/">Weather & climate</a>
    <a href="/visit/currency/">Currency & payments</a>
    <a href="/visit/attire/">Attire & dress code</a>
    <a href="/visit/transport/">Transport</a>
    <a href="/visit/accommodation/">Accommodation</a>
    <a href="/visit/communications/">Communications</a>
  </div>

  <div class="info-box">
    <h4>✈️ Nauru International Airport (INU)</h4>
    <p>The airport is compact and practical rather than polished. Expect a simple arrival process, limited facilities, and a quick transition to your hotel or guesthouse once you land. That simplicity is part of the island experience — but it means planning ahead matters.</p>
  </div>
</SubpageLayout>

<style>
  .callout-grid,.link-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:16px;margin:1.5rem 0}
